doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21316588
version: v1.0.1
title: "HARDENv2 / CGT-DAppSCAN: A Reproducible Bytecode Benchmark and Empirical Study of Smart-Contract Vulnerability Detectors"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lakadawala
    given-names: Hozefa
    affiliation: Binghamton University
  - family-names: Dzigbede
    given-names: Komla
    affiliation: Binghamton University
  - family-names: Chen
    given-names: Yu
    affiliation: Binghamton University
abstract: "CGT-DAppSCAN is a bytecode-level, multi-label smart-contract vulnerability benchmark of 2,186 Ethereum contracts across ten SWC weakness classes, with fixed splits, graph tensors, feature tables, and assessment masks. HARDENv2 is the heterogeneous-graph model family and evaluation pipeline used to compare graph transformers against tree ensembles, neural baselines, and Mythril on this benchmark."
